  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Daryeel: Stabilisation Support to Fragile Areas of Somalia II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project contributes to stability and peace by creating conditions for restoring trust horizontally between communities, and vertically between communities and local leadership in Somalia, aiming at rebuilding the social contract between Somali citizens and state institutions and providing a bridge to longer-term development interventions. Derived from experience on the ground, IOM identifies four pathways for addressing the most urgent stabilization needs in Somalia: implementing a dynamic pre- and post-recovery stabilization toolkit; facilitating &#x2018;government-led, community-driven&#x2019; action planning; enabling civic engagement in the absence of robust governance structures; and scaling-up grassroots inter-communal mediation efforts.</narrative>
  </description>
